<title>USA: Burlington, Hess bid on deep water blocks.</title>
<headline>Burlington, Hess bid on deep water blocks.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Burlington Resources Inc and Amerada Hess Corp -- biding jointly at the federal sale of outer continental shelf leases on Wednesday -- were the apparent high biders on 11 blocks primarily in the Garden Banks and East Breaks areas.</p>
<p>Burlington said on Thursday that its exposure on the 11 blocks is $2.7 million, while it has a $500,000 exposure on two blocks bid for its own account in the Garden Banks area.</p>
<p>It said Hess will operate blocks awarded as a result of the partners' joint bids.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.</p>
</text>
